Patagonia institutionalized repair as core brand strategy through its Worn Wear program combining in-store repairs, mail-in services, free DIY patch kits, and online repair guides co-created with iFixit. The company's repair team in Reno, Nevada processes thousands of garments annually, using repair data to inform product design improvements. This feedback loop ensures future products address common failure points. Patagonia's 'Ironclad' repair philosophy emphasizes emotional durability and product attachment, positioning repair as an expression of brand values. The integrated repair infrastructure generates competitive advantage through customer loyalty while reducing production volume, exemplifying product attachment as maintenance strategy.